Derived from QEMU 1:7.2+dfsg-7+deb12u18, softmmu/icount.c, accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-icount.c

Subject: icount: do not warp QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL over an unaccounted vCPU slice

icount_start_warp_timer() runs on the main thread (main_loop_wait,
timerlist_rearm) and, with -icount sleep=off, adds the precomputed distance
to the next QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL deadline onto qemu_icount_bias. The main
thread has current_cpu == NULL, and cpu->running is not set on the normal
exec path, so that clock is qemu_icount as of the last icount_update().

do_hlt() sets halted before the slice is published, so all_cpu_threads_idle()
is true while icount_budget is still the slice. icount_update_locked() then
does `budget -= executed` (a plain store, which is 0 when the slice ran to
completion) before the relaxed store of qemu_icount, both under
vm_clock_lock. An acquire load of icount_budget that does not take that lock
can observe 0 while qemu_icount still lags, and the warp overshoots by the
unpublished tail. Host scheduling decides whether the main thread samples
inside that window.

Skip the warp while any icount_budget is nonzero, and take vm_clock_lock
around that load. Do not sample the deadline and do not notify on the skip.
rr_cpu_thread_fn calls qemu_notify_event() after icount_process_data() when
every CPU is idle, and aio_compute_bh_timeout() turns that into a zero poll
timeout, so the warp is retried with a published clock. When every budget is
already 0 the existing `qemu_icount_bias += deadline` line is unchanged.

icount_decr and icount_extra are not read. The unpublished tail is
budget - (decr + extra), so it is nonzero only when budget is nonzero.
process_data clears decr and extra and then release-stores budget = 0 after
icount_update() returns; an acquire load that sees that 0 also sees the
published icount. A nonzero result only skips this attempt.

--- a/softmmu/icount.c
+++ b/softmmu/icount.c
@@ -310,6 +310,32 @@
     if (replay_mode != REPLAY_MODE_PLAY) {
         if (!all_cpu_threads_idle()) {
             return;
+        }
+
+        {
+            CPUState *cs;
+            bool unaccounted = false;
+
+            /*
+             * icount_update_locked stores `budget -= executed` (that store can
+             * be 0) before it stores qemu_icount, and both stores are covered
+             * by vm_clock_lock. Take that lock so this load cannot observe the
+             * 0 while the clock still lags. A nonzero budget is retried: the
+             * vCPU calls qemu_notify_event after icount_process_data.
+             */
+            seqlock_write_lock(&timers_state.vm_clock_seqlock,
+                               &timers_state.vm_clock_lock);
+            CPU_FOREACH(cs) {
+                if (qatomic_load_acquire(&cs->icount_budget) != 0) {
+                    unaccounted = true;
+                    break;
+                }
+            }
+            seqlock_write_unlock(&timers_state.vm_clock_seqlock,
+                                 &timers_state.vm_clock_lock);
+            if (unaccounted) {
+                return;
+            }
         }
 
         if (qtest_enabled()) {
--- a/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-icount.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-icount.c
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@
     /* Reset the counters */
     cpu_neg(cpu)->icount_decr.u16.low = 0;
     cpu->icount_extra = 0;
-    cpu->icount_budget = 0;
+    qatomic_store_release(&cpu->icount_budget, 0);
 
     replay_account_executed_instructions();
 
